Neighbor, I'm practically certain that the Dev-Team worries MUCH more
about what will make the code work on machine-n than about what is ANSI
standard. Some machines do not support signed char variables. On these
machines, the plusses to items and the AC are stored as signed shorts.
This is done by a typedef for type schar, which is NOT even mentioned
in the ANSI standard. I think that you MAY have to manually uncomment
the typedef for signed short and comment the one for signed char, but
in either case, the signed short version is IN THE DISTRIBUTION CODE!
It is part of the standard, although it is not normal. And in any 
case, an ANSI standard char is not defined in size, as I recall, but
only in that it must be able to identify a single character in the 
local character set. 8 bits is just normal. This last bit is drawn
from my foggy recollection, and is not by any means definitive.

Well, whatever.

